2. slows my review session*ÔSorry it has been unreliable and has slowed down your review sessions.
Background Auto Sync intentionally delays syncing while reviewing, while Anki is focused, or while dialogs are open. This is controlled under Tools â†’ Background Auto Sync Optionsâ€¦ â†’ Settings â†’ Interruption avoidance. You can disable Avoid sync while reviewing or increase/decrease the override timeout depending on your preferred behavior.
Version 5.0.0 also reduces repeated timer logging and writes the current session to auto_sync.log, which helps diagnose unreliable syncs. If the issue continues, please share the log from a session where the slowdown occurs, along with your Anki version and operating system, so I can investigate further.0ÌÎ€Ô¥Æ’lëåš
„Ç÷Ó"Unreliable. I often use the desktop app, leave it open, and then when I sync on mobile a day later it turns out that the last desktop session from the day before has been ignored. The logs are not helpful. It says: "Can't start sync timer (Main Window is not on deck browser or overview screen (state: review)â€”not sure what that means, but I know the app is not syncing correctly for some reason. *ìThanks for reporting this. The log message explains the behavior:
state: review
Anki is still on the reviewer screen, so Avoid sync while reviewing is intentionally preventing the background sync. The add-on does not consider the reviewer a safe state by default.
There is also a second setting that affects this use case. With Only sync when changes are detected enabled and When idle, sync every set to Off, the desktop app does not periodically poll AnkiWeb for changes made on mobile.
For a desktop replica that should update while left open:
1. Go to Tools â†’ Background Auto Sync Optionsâ€¦
2. Under Sync behavior, turn off Only sync when changes are detected, or configure When idle, sync every in the Background and network section.
3. Under Interruption avoidance, either disable Avoid sync while reviewing or set its override timeout so syncing is allowed after inactivity.
Version 5.0.0 also includes clearer effective-timeout logging and writes the current session to auto_sync.log. The message should be clearer in a future update, but state: review itself means the sync was deliberately deferred rather than failing.0ûÎ€Ô¥Æ’l°ıÖó(
