2026 - 08 - 11
Thanks for the detailed report â€” that was a great help! I've identified and fixed the issue.
Root cause: On AnkiMobile (iOS), there is no JavaScript API for revealing the answer. When you tapped an option, the add-on called pycmd('ans') (the reveal command used on Desktop). On iOS that call makes the WebView navigate to a blank page whose content is the literal text undefined â€” which is exactly why you saw the blank screen with "undefined" at the top. Your selection was still saved in the browser's session storage, which is why a second tap revealed the back side with the correct answer highlighted green.
It wasn't a problem on AnkiDroid because that call is silently ignored there and the app's own native "tap anywhere" did the reveal â€” hence AnkiDroid already working fine.
The fix (in v5.8.2+): On mobile, tapping an option now only saves your selection and lets AnkiMobile's native tap-to-reveal flip the card â€” no JavaScript reveal call is attempted, so no more undefined screen. Your choice still shows up green/red correctly on the back.
To get it on your phone:
1. Update the add-on, then go to Tools â†’ Add-ons â†’ AI-Hints â†’ Config â†’ Mobile Support â†’ (optionally Remove from All Note Types, then) One-Click Install: Setup All Note Types.
2. Sync Anki on your PC, then sync AnkiMobile.
3. Force-close AnkiMobile (swipe it away in the app switcher) and reopen it.
Important: since the flip now uses the native tap zones, keep Review â†’ Tap Zones â†’ When Question Shown â†’ "tap anywhere" â†’ Show Answer enabled (you already have this set, which is perfect).
Thanks again for reporting this â€” please let me know if the issue persists after updating!
--- original reply
1. Which app exactly are you on? (AnkiMobile for iPhone/iPad, or AnkiWeb in a mobile browser?) â€” AnkiDroid already works, so this is the critical differentiator.
2. When you tap an option, does the card flip to the answer side at all? (yes/no)
3. What does "undefined" look like exactly? Is it a popup/dialog, a small toast, text on the card, or nothing visible at all?
4. Where does "undefined" appear â€” immediately when tapping on the question side, or only after the answer is revealed?
5. Do the options show up at all? Can they tap "Show Options" and see the choices listed?
6. If they tap the same card again (blank area, not an option), does the answer reveal normally? (tests whether taps-to-show-answer are configured on AnkiMobile)
7. On AnkiMobile specifically: In Review â†’ tap zones in preferences, is "tap anywhere" set to "Show Answer"? (default)
8. A screenshot or screen recording of the "undefined" would be ideal if they can share one.

