ğ‚š–Ï"ßHey @athulkrishna2015
github does not have a issues page and the original addon doesn't seem to be being updated. My addon is bugging out and giving me this issue. [12:17:29] No internet connection, delaying sync for 0.9 minutes
Manual sync however works fine: 
[12:18:08] Sync initiated
[12:18:13] Sync completed

Do you have any insight in to a fix?*ıHi there! Thanks for reporting this issue.

I've investigated what's causing this, and the good news is that we've found the exact culprit and implemented a fix for it.

Why this is happening: Before initiating a background sync, the add-on explicitly tests for an active internet connection by trying to reach Google's DNS (8.8.8.8) on Port 53. While this works for the vast majority of users, many enterprise networks, university Wi-Fi, or restrictive routers actively intercept or block outbound traffic on Port 53 to prevent unauthorized DNS tunneling.

When you trigger a Manual Sync, Anki successfully connects to AnkiWeb over Port 443 (HTTPS), which is universally allowed by all firewalls. Because the add-on couldn't get a successful ping through Port 53, it assumed your internet was entirely down and backed off to avoid throwing errors.

The Fix: I have updated the add-on with two major improvements to solve this:

Smarter Connection Profiling: The network check now goes through Port 443 instead of 53, and features a robust fallback sequence that checks connectivity securely against ankiweb.net natively if the first ping fails.
New Configuration Option: We've added a new "Disable pre-sync internet check" toggle directly in the add-on's Options menu. If you are ever on an extremely strict firewall where even the fallback fails, you can toggle this setting on to skip the connectivity checks entirely and push straight into the sync.
These changes will be included in the next update. Thanks again for the report!0ˆÙ–Ï¥Æ’lû³ñî
